\item first proving that the solutions “concentrated at the origin as $\epsilon\to 0$ described in Theorem~A are non-degenerate”; 
\item then fixing “a sufficiently small $\epsilon>0$,” and combining these origin-concentrated solutions “with $k$ spikes in the vicinity of infinity to form a new approximate solution”;
