\begin{definition}[\bf Fit time]\label{df:fittime}
Let $(\xi_i,\zeta_i)_{i\geq 1}$  be a sequence of i.i.d. random variables according to $\al_{t,p,q}$ (Definition~\ref{df:alpha}). Suppose that $\Phi$ is an $\alpha_{t,p,q}$--ladder as in Lemma~\ref{lem:phi}. We say   $(\xi_i,\zeta_i)_{i\geq 1}$ has a \emph{fit time} at time $n$   for $m$ whenever the following are satisfied:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $n<\Phi_m$, 
\item $(\xi_n, \zeta_n)=(m, 0)$,
\item  $\xi_i<m$ for all $i<n$.
\end{enumerate}
\end{definition}

